WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
On a summer night, a
cricket chirps in the dark.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:08.770
Time its chirps on a warm night and on
a cool one, and you get different rates.

3
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.770
Chemical reactions change their
rates with temperature, too.

4
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.570
So could you measure an
activation energy with a cricket?

5
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.990
In this mission, you'll
meet the Arrhenius equation,

6
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.790
and see how the rate constant
changes with temperature.

7
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.790
You'll find activation energies from a
graph and from just two temperatures,

8
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.170
and find out what the
Arrhenius factor means.

9
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.430
Your mission: decide whether a cricket
could reveal an activation energy, and how.
